ToolForge-RL is an independent research project.

It studies ideas described by Tool-Star (RUC-NLPIR, MIT): tool-integrated
reasoning protocols, executable tool trajectories, and public reference
checkpoints/data. Tool-Star code or results must never be presented as results
of this project. The upstream source is pinned in
`data/manifests/source_manifest.json` and will live under
`third_party/Tool-Star/` only after Gate 0 passes.

Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct is used under the license supplied with its pinned model
revision. Public datasets retain their upstream licenses and attribution.
MATH-500 has no license field on its Hugging Face card at audit time; only IDs,
manifests, scripts, and small non-substitutive examples will be published until
redistribution terms are confirmed.

